  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "An electron accelerated through a potential difference <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has a de-Broglie wavelength of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>. When the potential is changed to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, its de-Broglie wavelength increases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0jL8r",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3Bluv",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NG7Dv",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "n3Mzj",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let initial wavelength be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>, then after&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;increase wavelength will become&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>.</p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>So we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>From both equations, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
